{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1144237-glamour-for-realms","id":1144237,"title":"Glamour for realms","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-26T17:40:26-07:00","id":1144237,"title":"Glamour for realms","content":"Question: when cheating realms with glamour does it cost one point per realm or 1 point per dot of a realm, my GM and i were trying to work that out, we both see in the arts section that it's per realm but we both remember it being per dot somewhere. Either way it's a bit messy, 1 per realm makes it very easy to destroy whole buildings or get eternally reoccurring cantrips and 1 per dot means that it's absurdly expensive to effect a base human or chimera if you don't already have those realms. We might homerule it to forbid modifier realms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T19:45:38-07:00","id":1144261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkfoxdev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1144237-glamour-for-realms#post1144237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: when cheating realms with glamour does it cost one point per realm or 1 point per dot of a realm, my GM and i were trying to work that out, we both see in the arts section that it's per realm but we both remember it being per dot somewhere. Either way it's a bit messy, 1 per realm makes it very easy to destroy whole buildings or get eternally reoccurring cantrips and 1 per dot means that it's absurdly expensive to effect a base human or chimera if you don't already have those realms. We might homerule it to forbid modifier realms.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1 per realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T19:52:47-07:00","id":1146222,"title":"","content":"My understanding is it is 1 per missing level of the realm. As in, if the third level of Actor is Familiar Face, and you have zero Actor normally, then to affect a news anchor you've seen on TV before, it would take 1 Glamour (to get that specific level of Actor that you don't have). If you have Scene and are going to affect a group of people, including a Thallain and an unfamiliar stranger, and you only have 1 Fae and 1 Actor, you spend 2 Glamour: one for Fae 4 (Elusive Gallain) and one for Actor 5 (Complete Stranger).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16478-tristerfalm","name":"tristerfalm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T21:35:15-07:00","id":1146250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tristerfalm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1144237-glamour-for-realms?p=1146222#post1146222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My understanding is it is 1 per missing level of the realm. As in, if the third level of Actor is Familiar Face, and you have zero Actor normally, then to affect a news anchor you've seen on TV before, it would take 1 Glamour (to get that specific level of Actor that you don't have). If you have Scene and are going to affect a group of people, including a Thallain and an unfamiliar stranger, and you only have 1 Fae and 1 Actor, you spend 2 Glamour: one for Fae 4 (Elusive Gallain) and one for Actor 5 (Complete Stranger).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nope its 1 per Realm. I","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T23:27:55-07:00","id":1146265,"title":"","content":"And my reading of it is that it's 1 per level actually used that you don't have. So if you have Fae 2 and use Fae 5 that's one, but if you use Fae 3 and Fae 5 that's two.<br /> <br /> Don't suppose we'll ever get clarity...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13395-daniel-knight","name":"Daniel Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T03:45:49-07:00","id":1146291,"title":"","content":"No, it\u2019s one per Realm. Lian is correct.<br /> <br /> Edit to add some examples for clarity: If you have Fae 1 but need Fae 5, that would be 1 Glamour point. If you have no Scene, but need 3, that would be one Glamour point. If you need both for the same cantrip, that would be 2 Glamour points to raise your Realms.<br /> <br /> You may still need to spend more Glamour on the cantrip for other requirements, but that\u2019s all you need to cheat Realms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":648,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","user":"PookaKnight","date":". 10-03-2017, 06:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T03:52:13-07:00","id":1146292,"title":"","content":"What <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar648_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"648\" data-vbnamecard=\"648\">PookaKnight</a> said.<br /> The examples in the book follows that course as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>__________________________________________________ </b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><i>Preaching the enlightened gospels of Gaming Anarchy</i></b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/225-growls","name":"Growls","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"292"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T17:58:15-07:00","id":1146502,"title":"","content":"Ok, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar648_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"648\" data-vbnamecard=\"648\">PookaKnight</a>, you said Lian was correct, who said that what I said was incorrect, but then you gave an example that's exactly what I was saying. So now I'm confused. Here's a different example. If I need to affect a group consisting of a Commoner, a Noble, and a Gallain, and I have zero Fae, do I spend 1 Glamour to get all of the Fae realm, or do I spend 3 Glamour, one for Fae 1 (for the Commoner), one for Fae 2 (for the Noble), and one for Fae 4 (for the Gallain)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16478-tristerfalm","name":"tristerfalm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T18:03:26-07:00","id":1146506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tristerfalm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1144237-glamour-for-realms?p=1146502#post1146502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar648_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"648\" data-vbnamecard=\"648\">PookaKnight</a>, you said Lian was correct, who said that what I said was incorrect, but then you gave an example that's exactly what I was saying. So now I'm confused. Here's a different example. If I need to affect a group consisting of a Commoner, a Noble, and a Gallain, and I have zero Fae, do I spend 1 Glamour to get all of the Fae realm, or do I spend 3 Glamour, one for Fae 1 (for the Commoner), one for Fae 2 (for the Noble), and one for Fae 4 (for the Gallain)?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You spend one extra for Fae, and One Extra for Scene assuming you have no scene. If you have some scene then 1 extra for Fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T19:13:20-07:00","id":1146522,"title":"","content":"What Lian says - Fae costs one Glamour. There\u2019s no need to spend multiple Glamour for multiple levels of the same Realm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-04T14:54:56-07:00","id":1146814,"title":"","content":"Can you also clarify what happens if you use Fae 2, Actor 3 and Scene 2 in one cantrip when you have all of them? What glamour and difficulty modifiers are applied?<br /> <br /> Much appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13395-daniel-knight","name":"Daniel Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}